<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103101" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεράμων</span></b>  (B) [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωνος</span></span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οντος</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ὁ</span> (?), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάλαμος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Anacr.
			</span></i> ap. Hilgard <i>Excerpta ex libris Herodiani</i> (Leipzig
				<i><span class="en">
				1887
			</span></i>) <i><span class="en">
				p.21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Sph.</u>
			</span></i> ibid.: v.
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Hermes</u>
				35.544
			</span></i>. (Said to be declined as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ντ-</span> stem by <i><span class="en">
				Anacr.
			</span></i> l.c. (this stem mentioned also by <i><span class="en">
				Arc.
				13
			</span></i>), but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ων -ωνος</span> by <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
			</span></i> l.c.: not found in our text of <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Sph.</u>
			</span></i>, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεράμωσι</span> (or perh.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεράμουσι</span>) is to be restored in
				<i><span class="en">
				221a
			</span></i> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλάμοις</span>.)</div>
